{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "description": "Declarative registry of binary-anchored offset detectors for RS3ProjectXUpdater. Each anchor maps one or more engine offsets (Offsets.kt) to a RELIABLE in-binary code location whose disassembly directly encodes the offset, plus a structural extraction recipe (the `extract` DSL). EXPORT fills sig_blob/sig_mask/feat_hash and resolves old_value against the OLD binary; IMPORT re-resolves against the NEW binary and flags drift (new_value != old_value). `old_value` is hand-seeded from the verified Offsets.kt and acts as a sanity bound. `validated:true` means the recipe was confirmed by hand against a live binary this session; `false` means seed/best-effort, to be confirmed by the export self-test (IMPORT against the source build must reproduce old_value).",
  "dsl": {
    "steps": [
      "find       {match, dst?, src?, mem?:{base,index,scale,disp}, imm?, occurrence?} \u2014 scan forward from entry for the Nth matching instruction; sets the cursor",
      "find_after {same as find} \u2014 scan forward from the current cursor (after the previous step)",
      "capture    {from:'mem.disp'|'imm', as:VAR} \u2014 record a displacement or immediate into VAR (attached to the matched instruction of the preceding find)",
      "rip_target {match, as:VAR} \u2014 capture the absolute resolved target of a RIP-relative MOV/LEA",
      "back_scan  {from_call:FUNC, match, mem:{base,...}, capture, occurrence?} \u2014 from a CALL to FUNC, scan backwards for a [base+disp] load",
      "call_arg   {call:FUNC, arg:N, capture} \u2014 capture disp of `LEA argRegN,[base+disp]` immediately before a CALL to FUNC"
    ],
    "operands": "register placeholders: '@name' binds a register on first use and refers to it after; '*' is wildcard. mem match fields are optional; scale/disp matched only when present.",
    "emit": "value is an integer expression over captured vars and hex/dec consts using + - * << (). One anchor may emit multiple offsets via emit[].",
    "manager_class": "ALTERNATIVE to anchor/extract: an anchor with {\"manager_class\":\"jag::SomeManager\",\"min_sites\":N,\"disp_min\":\"0x400\",\"disp_max\":\"0x20000\"} resolves by CONSENSUS \u2014 the tool scans every CALL to a method of that C++ class and reads the preceding `MOV/LEA RDI,[client+OFF]` this-load; the most common OFF (in [disp_min,disp_max], default 0x400-0x20000) wins. This is the most reliable OClient-pointer anchor (many independent callsites agree) and needs no anchor function. CRITICAL: keep disp_min high enough to exclude nested-object this-loads (this=[parent+0x20]) which can otherwise out-count the real client offset. min_sites guards weak consensus. Discover the class->offset map for a new build with `dump managers[:lo-hi]`; find where field-read managers are stored with `dump ctorstores:*@lo-hi`."
  },
  "ofunctions_note": "OFunctions consts -> qualified function name. IMPORT resolves each via the function sig-match (functions.ndjson) and emits the full OFunctions block into offsets_<ver>.kt. These are absolute function addresses (they move every build), so no drift flag.",
